                    <birth when="1794">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1855"/>
                    <occupation>Military Officer, Parliamentarian, </occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>A compatriot and fellow exile of Antonio Panizzi, who introduces him to Godwin, Evasio Radice came to
                            Britain in 1823, after the revolts against absolute power
                            in several of the Italian states between 1820 and 1823, in which he was active militarily. Having
                            fled to England following their suppression, he developed a career as a teacher, and became a naturalized citizen in 1837. 
                            In 1833 he married Maria Hutton, who belonged to the Norwich Unitarian
                            group. They had two children, Alberto (1836-1916) and Nina (1841-1866). He returned to Italy in 1848 and was elected to the Turin Parliament.
                            </p>
                    </note>
